v4l2codecs: request H.264 hardware transforms

Expose target output dimensions and clockwise rotation on the stateless H.264
decoder.  Apply V4L2_CID_ROTATE before COMPOSE so the requested dimensions are
in final orientation, and size the capture canvas to the requested target while
the driver reports the reachable active rectangle through G_SELECTION.

The H713 Cedrus implementation rounds each scale axis to 1, 1/2 or 1/4.  Thus
output-width=1280 output-height=720 requests a 1280x720 capture canvas and gets
a 960x544 active picture from 1920x1080 H.264.  The existing compose query then
advertises that active picture while preserving the larger allocation stride
and plane offsets.

Also honor the property ID offset that gst_v4l2_decoder_install_properties()
already accepts.  This leaves existing codecs unchanged and permits the H.264
class to install its own properties before the common device properties.

